     You don't have the latest version.  3.0 patchlevel 10 has a bug in
the game restore code that affects MSDOS, Atari, OS/2 (? not sure), and
AIX on RS6000 (for some but not all configurations).  With vanilla 3.0pl10,
if your system configuration is different at the time you restore than from
the time you saved, the object description data will become corrupted (and
that could produce even worse problems internally).  One possible work-around
would be to have a NetHack-specific boot configuration that you always use
before starting the game.  (Perhaps a bit drastic, but should work fine.)

     There was an "unofficial" patch posted to fix this, and the binaries
available from linc.cis.upenn.edu were updated to include that fix or a
comparable one.  (Back in March or thereabouts.)  That patch is available
in pub/NH3.0/PC there; I don't remember the file name.  The description
claims that it's only for MSDOS, but that's not true; it's needed for a
few others (see above) and it won't hurt anybody who doesn't need it (Unix
other than AIX, VMS, Mac, Amiga).

